{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"operations\":[{\"operation\":\"UPDATE\",\"target_ids\":[\"nda-definition-and-communication-scope\"],\"skill\":{\"id\":\"nda-definition-and-communication-scope\",\"hypothesis_ids\":[\"nda-1\",\"nda-2\",\"nda-3\"],\"guidance\":{\"inspection\":\"Reconstruct the complete operative protected-information definition, including incorporated definitions, preambles, alternatives, exclusions, and form conditions. For explicit identification, test the universal requirement: reasonable-understanding, nature, circumstances, or automatic-inclusion alternatives contradict it; silence is NotMentioned. Express nontechnical subjects contradict technical-only scope. Express oral or verbal inclusion entails verbal coverage even if confirmation is required. Preserve every independently responsive definition and alternative.\",\"historical_example_refs\":[\"416:nda-1\",\"416:nda-2\",\"416:nda-3\"]}},\"source_case_ids\":[416],\"rationale\":\"Retains the parent boundary while emphasizing universal quantifiers, indirect definitional chains, and complete evidence membership; one shared full-context demonstration controls representation cost.\"},{\"operation\":\"UPDATE\",\"target_ids\":[\"nda-permissions-exceptions-and-rights\"],\"skill\":{\"id\":\"nda-permissions-exceptions-and-rights\",\"hypothesis_ids\":[\"nda-15\",\"nda-12\",\"nda-13\",\"nda-7\",\"nda-5\",\"nda-4\"],\"guidance\":{\"inspection\":\"Locate an operative permission, exclusion, restriction, or reservation and verify actor, object, recipient class, purpose, polarity, and conditions. Keep independent development distinct from lawful third-party receipt. Sharing needs an operative disclosure or access rule plus incorporated class definitions; an exclusive employee-only rule contradicts nonemployee sharing. Limited use requires a use restriction, not purpose-limited copying or disclosure. No-licensing requires an express no-right, ownership, or reservation rule; access alone is unresolved.\",\"historical_example_refs\":[\"416:nda-15\",\"416:nda-7\",\"416:nda-4\"]}},\"source_case_ids\":[416],\"rationale\":\"Repairs recurring substitutions between development and acquisition, access and licensing, and employee versus nonemployee permissions without adding unsupported vocabulary requirements.\"},{\"operation\":\"UPDATE\",\"target_ids\":[\"nda-information-lifecycle-and-continuity\"],\"skill\":{\"id\":\"nda-information-lifecycle-and-continuity\",\"hypothesis_ids\":[\"nda-16\",\"nda-17\",\"nda-20\",\"nda-19\"],\"guidance\":{\"inspection\":\"Read each return, destruction, copying, retention, and survival clause with its trigger, lead-in, alternatives, exceptions, and cross-references. Return-or-destruction needs a mandatory disposition tied within the operative rule to termination or a comparable contractual end; a request-only duty remains NotMentioned. Copy permission must be affirmative; consent-dependent prohibition contradicts it. Post-disposition possession requires an express retention exception, while an unqualified all-material duty contradicts it. Survival requires an identified obligation continuing after an end event.\",\"historical_example_refs\":[\"416:nda-16\",\"416:nda-20\"]}},\"source_case_ids\":[416],\"rationale\":\"Targets observed relation errors involving request-only return duties, consent-based copying prohibitions, and unqualified return obligations while preserving full trigger and exception evidence.\"},{\"operation\":\"UPDATE\",\"target_ids\":[\"nda-special-disclosure-and-conduct-controls\"],\"skill\":{\"id\":\"nda-special-disclosure-and-conduct-controls\",\"hypothesis_ids\":[\"nda-10\",\"nda-8\",\"nda-18\",\"nda-11\"],\"guidance\":{\"inspection\":\"Inspect the complete document for four separate controls. Agreement confidentiality includes nondisclosure of the agreement, its existence or terms, or discussions or negotiations; a direct sentence is sufficient, while definition-based coverage also needs the secrecy duty. Compelled-disclosure notice needs legal or governmental compulsion linked to notice or consultation. Preserve all operative personnel and corpus-supervised proxy-solicitation restrictions with lead-ins and exceptions. Reverse engineering requires an operative reverse-engineering, decompilation, or disassembly prohibition; absence of a clause is only NotMentioned.\",\"historical_example_refs\":[\"416:nda-10\",\"416:nda-8\"]}},\"source_case_ids\":[416],\"rationale\":\"Corrects missed direct agreement-confidentiality evidence and keeps notice, solicitation, and reverse-engineering tests distinct without treating retrieval absence as proof.\"}],\"noop_reason\":null}"}}
